  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#356\", \"PowerToys#38791\", \"PowerToys#7260\"], \"answer\": \"The folder-size part of this request has been reported before. PowerToys#356 is the main open thread, and the other tickets were closed as duplicates of it. PowerToys has no feature that shows folder sizes in File Explorer's Details view yet, so there's nothing to enable. Add your use case and a thumbs-up to #356 so it gets tracked there. In the meantime, use a third-party tool such as WinDirStat, WizTree, the Folder Size shell extension, or the Files app to see which folders use the most space. The archive has separate tickets asking for custom folder colors, such as #6157 and #9891. I found no ticket that asks for colors based on size, so that part may be new. Add it as a comment on #356.\"}",
